## Feature 7: School Data from School Websites — Built

- **US7.1 (Kidscover Admin):** As an admin, I want the system to read each school's own website and suggest its board, levels, admission status, facilities and claimed achievements, each with the sentence and page it came from.
- **US7.2 (Kidscover Admin):** As an admin, I want to accept or reject each suggestion (strong ones ticked, weak ones not), and accept CBSE boards confirmed by CBSE's record in bulk.
- **US7.3 (Backend):** As a system, I need to read politely (robots.txt, a few pages, size and time limits), safely (no private addresses, redirects re-checked), and in English, Marathi and Hindi; to confirm CBSE affiliation numbers against CBSE's record; and never to overwrite what a school entered itself.
- **US7.4 (Parent):** As a parent, I want to see where each fact came from and when it was checked.

---

## Feature 8: School Profiles, School Staff & the Change Log — Built

- **US8.1 (Kidscover Admin):** As an admin, I want to give a school's staff access to edit their own school's page, by email.
- **US8.2 (School Admin):** As a school's staff member, I want to upload our photo (confirming we may publish it), list our facilities (with details such as our teacher-student ratio) and our achievements (results, placements, alumni, awards), and see our change history.
- **US8.3 (Kidscover Admin):** As an admin, I want to see every change any school makes (who, when, before and after) and undo any of them, so the data stays accurate.
- **US8.4 (Kidscover Admin):** As an admin, I want to find free-licensed photos of a school on Wikimedia Commons and use one with its author and licence.
- **US8.5 (Backend):** As a system, I need the change log written by database triggers (so nothing escapes it), edits allowed only through functions that check the school, and a photo bucket where each school can write only to its own folder.
- **US8.6 (Kidscover Admin / School Admin):** As an admin or a school's staff member, I want to set the school's levels by hand when the automatic ones are missing ("Level not stated") or wrong, and hand it back to the automatic levels later, with every change in the change log.

